From efb5edce3be9bacfece3035ed0ab73d1453f73d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: curnane-lab <227407786+curnane-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:00:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(gdn): route spec-decode verify through the recover
 operator behind VLLM_ASCEND_GDN_RECOVER

Experimental same-acceptance-trajectory A/B wiring (evaluation N10): with
VLLM_ASCEND_GDN_RECOVER=1 the pure spec-decode verify call in gdn.py uses
aclnnRecurrentGatedDeltaRuleRecover (via the installed fla_npu ctypes
runtime; kernel binaries from ASCEND_CUSTOM_OPP_PATH) with a per-layer
records workspace and per-token record indices. source_state stays null,
keeping the stock in-place read semantics (bit-identical by design), so the
R1-3 source/destination overlap rule does not apply. num_accepted_tokens is
clamped to [1, num_spec+1]. Mixed batches and non-uniform windows fall back
to the stock operator (counted in gdn_recover.FALLBACKS). Off by default;
stock path is byte-identical.

Signed-off-by: curnane-lab <227407786+curnane-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
